Subject: [PATCH 15/17] =?utf-8?q?media:=20nv=5Fvideo=20ABI=202=20with=20th?=
 =?utf-8?q?e=20Codec2=20core=20=E2=80=94=20picture=20count,=20size-change?=
 =?utf-8?q?=20re-creation,=20HDR=20static=20info?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

nv_video (driver-source/native video tree):
- ABI 2: nv_video_decode returns the displayable pictures a unit produced
  (success is rc >= 0); NV_VIDEO_E_RESIZE + nv_video_required_size for a
  random access point larger than the session; nv_video_picture_hdr.
- VP9 segment maps: zeroed once with the side buffer at allocation, read/write
  pair swapped only after segmentation_update_map, nothing touched at
  key/intra-only/error-resilient pictures (the engine applies the reset).
- HEVC 2-D tile grids, H.264/HEVC/AV1/VP9 refusals with named reasons,
  HDR static metadata parser (SEI 137/144, AV1 HDR_MDCV/HDR_CLL).

Codec2 core: rc >= 0 is success; a unit that produced no picture is finished
at once; E_RESIZE drains the old session, re-creates it at the new size,
replays in-band parameter sets and decodes the unit again (AOSP
C2SoftHevcDec.cpp:881-890 precedent); HDR static metadata per output.
Component: C2StreamHdrStaticInfo declared and reported (buffer info +
configUpdate on change), coded units converted per codec.

Verified: core_test + xml_test pass (stub covers count, retire, resize with
and without buffer backpressure, HDR units); realtest-all 9/9 PASS on the
RTX 5090; android-c2 compiles; native lib tests 46 video pass.

(cherry picked from commit fbcc0669d9b41c79e1dd27b1601d02b15cd17f05)
